  "observations": [
    "Selecting Button creates a separate real visual-only Unit model; Add still attaches Button to the current host draft and repeated Add does not duplicate it.",
    "Selecting Angle disposes the previous preview; closing the catalog removes and disposes its shell; reopening creates a fresh preview without changing the host draft.",
    "A barrier delays the real Relay model module response. Selecting Button before release keeps Button current, and the stale Relay shell is actually disposed.",
    "Changing the main device preserves the same standalone preview object and refreshes the selected Unit note/capability; each host retains its own draft.",
    "A real canvas click on the standalone preview while viewing a borrowed HTTP-fixture session does not attach the draft to that session or produce session writes.",
    "Page navigation invokes the actual pagehide preview disposal; Token helper is associated with its input using aria-describedby.",
    "Existing invalid-draft rejection, load/cancel locking, uncertain-stop fences, borrowed-session no-create/delete behavior, and delayed device/session race contracts remain included."
